        "Text": {
          "type": "cexolocstring",
          "value": {
            "0": "At minimum, you need to define one fish. To define the fish, call:\n\nAddFish(X, \"Y\");\n\nX is how often the fish nibbles at the player's hook and Y is a comma-separated list of fish. For example, to define a common bass and trout along with a rare sturgeon, use the following:\n\nAddFish(50, \"bass, trout\");\nAddFish(5, \"sturgeon\");\n\nThe bass and trout will each bite 50% of the time, while the sturgeon will only bite 5% of the time."
          }
        }
